  "id": "Compound::DB00234 - Gene::6530",
  "verbalization": "Reboxetine is linked to Slc6a2 through a series of molecular and pharmacological interactions. The evidence suggests that Reboxetine, through its effects on blood pressure and urethral pain, indirectly influences Slc6a2 via the neurotransmitter dextroamphetamine and levomilnacipran, both of which bind to Slc6a2. The common ancestors of these pathways—Agent Affecting Nervous System and Organooxygen Compound—highlight a potential role in neurochemical regulation. The integration of these pathways implies that Reboxetine may modulate Slc6a2 through a mechanism involving neurotransmitter binding and systemic effects, potentially impacting ion transport across cell membranes. The evidence supports a role for Reboxetine in influencing Slc6a2 through a network of pharmacological and biochemical interactions, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
